# Netlify-only: excludes these paths from the deployed/uploaded bundle
# without touching git. The GitHub Action (build-content.yml) regenerates
# and commits the real pages BEFORE Netlify ever runs, and Netlify has no
# separate build command for this site — it just uploads the publish
# directory (the repo root) as-is. templates/ holds the raw page-template
# sources ({{tokens}}, not meant to be public) that scripts/build.py reads
# from; keeping them in git is required (that's the whole CMS pipeline),
# but there's no reason for them to ever reach the CDN. Belt-and-suspenders
# with the forced _redirects rule below: this keeps the files off the
# deploy entirely, so there's nothing left for a redirect rule to have to
# out-rank. templates-page/ (the real Templates shop page's own output
# directory) is a different, unrelated name and is not touched by this.
templates/
